這段文字是心理懸疑小說《沉默的病人》（The Silent Patient）的開頭。以下為您整理成「英文一句、中文一句」的對照：
ALICIA BERENSON WAS THIRTY-THREE YEARS OLD when she killed her husband.
艾莉西亞・貝倫森（Alicia Berenson）謀殺丈夫時年三十三歲。
They had been married for seven years.
他們結婚七年了。
They were both artists—Alicia was a painter, and Gabriel was a well-known fashion photographer.
兩人都是藝術家——艾莉西亞是畫家，蓋布瑞（Gabriel）則是知名的時尚攝影師。
He had a distinctive style, shooting semi-starved, semi-naked women in strange, unflattering angles.
他有獨特的風格，專門拍攝半飢餓、半裸的女性，角度奇特且不討喜。
Since his death, the price of his photographs has increased astronomically.
自他死後，他的攝影作品價格暴漲。
I find his stuff rather slick and shallow, to be honest.
老實說，我覺得他的東西相當圓滑而膚淺。
It has none of the visceral quality of Alicia’s best work.
它完全沒有艾莉西亞優秀作品那種直擊人心的力量。
I don’t know enough about art to say whether Alicia Berenson will stand the test of time as a painter.
我對藝術了解不夠深，無法斷言艾莉西亞・貝倫森身為畫家是否禁得起時間的考驗。
Her talent will always be overshadowed by her notoriety, so it’s hard to be objective.
她的才華永遠會被她的惡名所掩蓋，所以很難做到客觀。
And you might well accuse me of being biased.
而你大可指責我有偏見。
All I can offer is my opinion, for what it’s worth.
我能提供的只有我的看法，儘管它或許微不足道。
And to me, Alicia was a kind of genius.
但在我眼裡，艾莉西亞堪稱某種天才。
Apart from her technical skill, her paintings have an uncanny ability to grab your attention—by the throat, almost—and hold it in a viselike grip.
除了精湛的技藝外，她的畫作還有一種不可思議的力量，能抓住你的注意力——簡直像掐住你的喉嚨一樣——並用虎鉗般的緊握力將其扣留。
